<title>ITALY: Italy's Banca di Roma is overstaffed -- report.</title>
<headline>Italy's Banca di Roma is overstaffed -- report.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-10-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The chairman of Italy's Banca di Roma was quoted as saying that the bank had as many as 3,500 excess employees on its books.</p>
<p>Italian banks would have to reduce staff &quot;if we want Italian banks to stay competitive and produce enough income to finance their growth,&quot; Geronzi told business weekly Il Mondo, published at the weekend.</p>
<p>Geronzi said that the entire Banca di Roma group had a surplus of between 3,000 and 3,500 employees.</p>
<p>He said banks had to be given the freedom to offer more flexible contractual terms to employees such as part-time work.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392-66102321</p>
